Cell["\<\
Use gray[n] for a gray group. Type-I, type-III, and type-IV groups use \
complete BNS pairs: typeI[{n,m}], typeIII[{n,m}], and typeIV[{n,m}].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fe6e2b20-5435-467c-8d96-9a0620ea1eb3"],

Cell["\<\
Each returned item is {label,R,t,flag}: R and t are the point and translation \
parts in fractional coordinates, and flag states whether the operation is \
unitary or antiunitary.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3bf15d89-7a86-445d-a55f-0365d6a46e98"],

Cell["\<\
The list may be passed directly to symminformation in init. Its order is also \
the order used when displaying the corresponding representation matrices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"edebe537-c04d-473f-b5e5-aaf0a8e7500d"]
}, Closed]],

